{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794826598,"nonce":"EVBUmiSBPfryvYu9bo03kjSCdq0=","message":"Default backend per platform, decided 2026-11-16: GpuDevice.defaultBackends() orders the compiled-in backends by platform. Apple platforms: Metal, Vulkan, GLES. Windows: Direct3D 12, Vulkan, GLES. Other native platforms: Vulkan, GLES. The browser (emscripten or wasm builds): WebGPU, WebGL2. A compiled-in backend the platform list leaves out comes after. Overrides, from strongest: OpenOptions.backends in code; HXN_GPU_BACKEND at run time, as a comma-separated list such as vulkan,gles; -D hxn_gpu_backend at compile time, whose names Setup checks are compiled in. Checked on macOS under Ash: default Metal, HXN_GPU_BACKEND=vulkan and gles,metal, and the errors for a backend that is not compiled in and for an unknown name. In Chrome: WebGPU by default with both web drivers, and WebGL2 with -D hxn_gpu_backend=webgl2.","files":null}]}